EFG 2 R "Kohlberg and Mertens (1986), Figure 10" { "I" "II" }
"A presentation of the game :math:`\Delta` showing that stable sets need not satisfy backwards induction. The set of equilibria containing (T,(1/4,3/4)) and (T,(3/4,1/4)) is stable, but in this presentation the unique sequential equilibrium is (T,(1/2,1/2)).

Player I chooses T, which ends the game with payoffs (1,-1), or continue; he then chooses M or B; player II, not told which, chooses L or R. The payoffs are those of the matrix game :math:`\Delta`."

